+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 4. Geometry: how do the dimensions relate in embedding space? (structural validity)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "High cosine similarity between two probe directions means LaBSE, trained on HESEIA's items, represents the two dimensions in nearly the same way. Gender identity vs. sexual orientation is the pair to watch; your brainstorming notes ask whether they are \"related or siloed\"."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "sim = ip.direction_similarity({d: probes[d] for d in usable_heseia})\n",
+    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6, 5))\n",
+    "im = ax.imshow(sim.values, cmap=\"RdBu_r\", vmin=-1, vmax=1)\n",
+    "ax.set_xticks(range(len(sim)), sim.index, rotation=45, ha=\"right\", fontsize=8)\n",
+    "ax.set_yticks(range(len(sim)), sim.index, fontsize=8)\n",
+    "for s in ax.spines.values(): s.set_visible(False)\n",
+    "fig.colorbar(im, ax=ax, label=\"cosine similarity of probe directions\", shrink=0.8)\n",
+    "ax.set_title(\"HESEIA identity directions in LaBSE\", loc=\"left\", fontsize=11)\n",
+    "fig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(OUT / \"probe_direction_similarity.png\", dpi=200); plt.show()\n",
+    "sim"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 5. Transfer check on BBQ: can HESEIA's probes be read on BBQ at all?\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Each probe is applied to BBQ items (from notebook 01) and scored against BBQ's **own** harmonized labels. Intersection labels count for both parts. Two readings are possible, and the controls tell them apart:\n",
+    "- **low transfer because of language/format**: the transfer also fails on **EsBBQ** (Spanish, same format as BBQ) or improves after per-language centering → a technical shift, not a finding;\n",
+    "- **low transfer despite controls**: HESEIA's and BBQ's operationalizations of that dimension diverge → evidence for RQ2.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Both views are compared. If transfer works only on **unmasked** BBQ, the probes rely on identity words rather than stereotype content."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "from benchbias.schema import CROSSWALK\n",
+    "BBQ = {}\n",
+    "for v in [\"masked\", \"unmasked\"]:\n",
+    "    df = pd.read_parquet(OUT / f\"bbq_{v}_clusters.parquet\")       # written by notebook 01, §10\n",
+    "    Xb = np.load(OUT / f\"bbq_{v}_labse.npy\")\n",
+    "    S = ip.score(Xb, probes)\n",
+    "    BBQ[v] = dict(df=df, X=Xb, S=S, harmonized=df[\"category\"].map(CROSSWALK[\"BBQ\"]))\n",
+    "\n",
+    "transfer = pd.concat({v: ip.transfer_check(BBQ[v][\"S\"], BBQ[v][\"harmonized\"]) for v in BBQ}, axis=1)\n",
+    "transfer"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "# Robustness: remove the language offset (HESEIA = es, BBQ = en) and re-check transfer\n",
+    "Xall = np.vstack([X, BBQ[\"masked\"][\"X\"]])\n",
+    "Xc = ip.center_by_group(Xall, [\"es\"] * len(X) + [\"en\"] * len(BBQ[\"masked\"][\"X\"]))\n",
+    "probes_c = ip.fit_probes(Xc[: len(X)], Y)\n",
+    "S_c = ip.score(Xc[len(X):], probes_c)\n",
+    "pd.concat({\"raw\": transfer[(\"masked\", \"transfer_AUC\")],\n",
+    "           \"language-centered\": ip.transfer_check(S_c, BBQ[\"masked\"][\"harmonized\"])[\"transfer_AUC\"]}, axis=1)"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "usable_bbq = [d for d in usable_heseia\n",
+    "              if transfer.get((\"masked\", \"transfer_AUC\"), pd.Series(dtype=float)).get(d, np.nan) >= MIN_TRANSFER_AUC]\n",
