+    "# Dimensions with no BBQ counterpart (e.g. profession, geographic_origin) have no transfer AUC.\n",
+    "# They can still be projected, but read them descriptively: 'how much of HESEIA's X is in this cluster'."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 6. Cluster profiles: which dimension drives each BBQ cluster?\n",
+    "\n",
+    "For each cluster from notebook 01: the mean probe score per dimension, the **driver** (highest dimension), its **margin** over the runner-up, and BBQ's own dominant category. Disagreements are the interesting rows. A small margin means the cluster is driven by no single dimension, which may itself be a sign of intersectional or mixed content."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "profiles = {}\n",
+    "for v in BBQ:\n",
+    "    profiles[v] = ip.cluster_profiles(BBQ[v][\"S\"], BBQ[v][\"df\"][\"cluster\"],\n",
+    "                                      native=BBQ[v][\"harmonized\"], usable=usable_bbq or None)\n",
+    "    profiles[v].to_csv(OUT / f\"cluster_profiles_bbq_{v}.csv\")\n",
+    "p = profiles[\"masked\"]\n",
+    "print(\"driver == BBQ's own category:\", (p[\"driver\"] == p[\"native_dominant\"]).mean().round(3))\n",
+    "p.sort_values(\"driver_margin\").head(20)"
+   ]
